/* Data for Animal-Crossing-Villager-Data-Reports.html (TECHNICAL §4.18). Four sources, kept as published so
   js/analyst.js can check and join them in the visitor’s browser:

   VILLAGERS_CSV  The villagers.csv the Kaggle notebook reads: the “Animal Crossing New Horizons
                  Nookplaza” dataset, 391 villagers. Columns kept: Name, Species, Gender,
                  Personality, Hobby, Birthday, Catchphrase, Favorite Song, Style 1, Style 2,
                  Color 1, Color 2 and Filename (the game's own ID for each villager, used to
                  find their picture in img/villagers/). Furniture, wallpaper and flooring left out.
   WISH_TXT       ac_vil_ranking.txt: the Nook Market “most wished for” villager list, scraped
                  from the web page (May 2020), raw. Website text is still in it on purpose:
                  the cleaning happens on the page, where the checks can show it.
   TIER_CSV       acnh_villager_data.csv (from archive.zip): a fan tier list, tiers 1 to 6.
   VILLAGERS_TT_CSV  The TidyTuesday copy (VillagerDB, 2020-05-05) of the same villagers, used
                  only to compare the two copies.

   Pictures: img/villagers/icon/<Filename>.webp and img/villagers/photo/<Filename>.webp, the
   game's icons and photos from the ACNH API fan project (github.com/alexislours/ACNHAPI),
   which names each file by the same ID. Converted to WebP; nothing drawn or changed.

   Animal Crossing and its characters are trademarks of Nintendo; the pictures are Nintendo's.
   Fan data, used for a practice analysis. */
